	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Numerical variables were not transformed, categorical variables were one-hot encoded, and missing values were not imputed because “XGBoost treats missing data as a specific modality.” PGD3-T72 occurred in 83 of 477 recipients, but no class weighting, over-sampling, under-sampling, or other explicit imbalance method was reported. The primary XGBoost train/test split proportion and corresponding counts were not stated. The authors report that their “full codebase has been made publicly available.”

