	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The primary outcome was grade 3 primary graft dysfunction at 72 hours according to the 2016 ISHLT definition. The optimal six-feature XGBoost model was evaluated at step 8, immediately after second graft implantation, and achieved a median AUROC of 0.84 with an IQR of 0.065; the abstract reports sensitivity 0.81 and specificity 0.68. Although bootstrap confidence intervals were said to have been generated, numeric lower and upper 95% CI limits were not reported. Accuracy, PPV, NPV, and F1-score were not provided in the main paper. The authors qualitatively described superior or well-calibrated risk estimates, but no calibration intercept, slope, Brier score, or calibration plot was reported. DCA was not reported.

